Nox is the being whose body lies in the mines beneath [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Umbervale Hold|Umbervale Hold]] in [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]]. Blood taken from the body, noxblood, is the source of [[Phenomena/Althane/Sanguis Noxa|vampirism]], and it is what Oreskian expeditions descend into the mines to find.

Nox is a [[Divinity/Thessians|Thessian]] of night and darkness, of the second generation, one of the older and more abstract of them. The first generation are [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Harrow|the one called Leitmotif]] and the Deeper; Nox is second, Beast third, and Mephi and Muriel fourth. It is not dormant. [[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] met it as a vast bundle of black silk hanging in a cold, colorless place, and it spoke to him as intent rather than words. It took his service, wrapping a strip of its silk around his arm, and it does not concern itself with the cabal that drinks its blood.

[[People/Althane/Lev|Lev]] later agreed to be its Herald and mortal avatar, and the bond shows: a soul-scanner reads a quarter of his soul as the same black silk, and the rest of him is slowly taking on its bearing.
